				April 19, 1985

	In going to version 4 of VMS, DEC has removed a feature
	of the LINKER and IMAGE ACTIVATOR which causes the
	current versions of STOIC and RED to fail with a BADISD
	message upon startup.

	To make STOIC & RED work under VMS Ver. 4, edit the file,
	[SAOSTOIC.STOIC]IMAGE.
	After the line:
'IMAGE_WRT : -1 .IMAGE ;  % also allow for writable images
	insert the following lines
'IMAGE :
  "Creating writable image." MSG CR
  "If installing in system, do not use /SHARE switch." MSG CR
  IMAGE
  ;
	Then execute the procedure [SAOSTOIC]STOBUILD.
	This will result in a version of STOIC & RED which is not
	"sharable".  The only effect is a reduction in efficiency
	in heavily loaded systems with multiple RED users.  I will
	create a working sharable version when we bring up VMS Ver. 4
	at the CfA.

	If this version is to be installed by the system manager
	of a VMS system as a known image using the procedure,
	[SAOSTOIC]INSTALL.COM, the last line of that procedure
	should have "/SHARE" deleted.

	I have successfully (but briefly) used this version of RED/STOIC
	on the Faculty VAX at Northeastern University where they are
	using VMS 4.1.  I have not tried installing it because I do
	not have the privilege to do so on that machine.

	I am interested in immediate feedback if problems are encountered.
	I will respond quickly to such reports.

				Roger Hauck
				Center for Astrophysics
				(Smithsonian Astrophysical Observatory)
